# Medioo site blocks, copied read-only from the box on 2026-10-21 (DR-40, plan task X1).
#
# Source of truth: until W1c, the box is the source — /home/ec2-user/n8n/Caddyfile on the EC2 host, which also
# holds the n8n ({$DOMAIN}) and bddrug (drugdb.eliooo.org) blocks; those are deliberately not copied here. One reload
# affects all three tenants. From W1c on, the box's medioo/baymax blocks are pasted from THIS file. Editing this file
# routes nothing by itself: a path reaches medioo-web only once it is routed in the box's Caddyfile.
#
# Drift: nothing detects it automatically until W1c adds the check to the post-deploy smoke. Before pasting from
# this file, diff its blocks against the live Caddyfile's medioo/baymax blocks; any difference is a box edit to fold
# in here first, never to overwrite.
#
# Editing the box. /home/ec2-user/n8n/Caddyfile is bind-mounted into n8n-caddy-1 as a SINGLE FILE (read-only inside
# the container). Anything that replaces the inode — sed -i, mv of a temp file, rsync, an editor that saves by
# rename — leaves the container reading the old file, and `caddy reload` then quietly reloads the stale config.
#   cd /home/ec2-user/n8n
#   cp Caddyfile Caddyfile.bak-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M)
#   cat /path/to/new-Caddyfile > Caddyfile                     # in place only; never sed -i, mv or rsync
#   docker exec n8n-caddy-1 cat /etc/caddy/Caddyfile | diff - Caddyfile          # must print nothing
#   docker exec n8n-caddy-1 caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile        # must say Valid configuration
#   docker exec n8n-caddy-1 caddy reload --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#   curl -sI https://medioo.eliooo.org/ ; curl -sI https://drugdb.eliooo.org/ ; curl -sI https://<n8n host>/
#     -> compare each status code with the one recorded before the edit; any change means restore the backup
#        (cat Caddyfile.bak-... > Caddyfile) and reload.
#
# Headers: deleting `-Server` makes Caddy defer this header block to response-write time, so the values below
# OVERWRITE whatever the upstream sends. Caddy is therefore the owner of HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options and
# Referrer-Policy on every path, Java's or Next's; an upstream that sets a different Referrer-Policy is overruled.
#
# DR-40 A1: Java is the default. A path goes to medioo-web:3000 only once it is listed here and applied on the box.
# Flipping a route back is a one-line edit plus the procedure above.

medioo.eliooo.org {
	encode zstd gzip

	header {
		Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
		X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
		Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
		-Server
	}

	reverse_proxy medscribe-ai:8086
}

# Old public name (DR-15, 2026-09-19): every URL already sent to families keeps working via a permanent redirect.
baymax.eliooo.org {
	redir https://medioo.eliooo.org{uri} permanent
}
